WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language:  en

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.500
Bad Voice: Here's to another shitty day, Mr.
Entrepreneur, Mr. Future Millionaire.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.320
Good Voice: What is wrong with you?

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.670
Do you wake up every single day this negative?

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.820
Bad Voice: [Sigh] Oh, man, what a day today
is, huh?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:28.920
Mmmm.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.640
... Dude, do you want a beer?

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.100
Good Voice: It's 7:00 in the morning.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.860
Bad Voice: So what, man, that's the best time
of the day to drink.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.500
On an empty stomach, it's a lot cheaper.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.059
You know, there was a study done once, saying
it's 50% cheaper to drink in the morning than

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:47.059
in the afternoon.

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:48.739
I'm just trying to save you some money, man.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:49.879
Good Voice: Oh yeah?

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:50.879
Who did that study?

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:53.510
Bad Voice: Uh, it was an extensive study done
by Playboy magazine.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.280
Good Voice: Great selection of reading material.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.370
Bad Voice: You know, it really is.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.559
I've learned so much from them.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:00:58.910
I mean, the content is ridiculous.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.820
They teach you different positions, you know,
different pickup lines.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.820
You should subscribe.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.820
It's very good.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:04.820
Good Voice: Yeah, I'll pass.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:05.820
Bad Voice: Whatever.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:06.320
It's up to you.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.720
Bad Voice: [cough, cough] Loser.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.000
[Radio goes on, playing Tony Robbins.]

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.560
Good Voice: Oh, thank you.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.040
That is music to my ears.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.180
Bad Voice: Wait a minute.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:19.740
Are we really doing to listen to this?

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:20.740
No Kanye West?

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.400
We have to sit here and listen to this Tim
Robbins guy?

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.530
Good Voice: Uh, it's Tony Robbins.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.570
Tim Robbins is an actor.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.229
Bad Voice: Whatever, Tony, Tim, it's the same
guy.

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:32.640
It's the same dude that gets up and says,
"Personal power!

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.470
Live with passion!

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.869
Get the edge!"

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:37.810
Have you ever thought about why this guy's
so excited?

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:41.860
Bad Voice: He's excited because people pay
$200 to listen to this crap.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.100
I'd be excited, too.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.020
Good Voice: [Chuckles] You know, I find you
so entertaining on some of the stuff you say.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.840
Pat, you do not have to listen to what he's
telling you.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.520
Sometimes the life of an entrepreneur's filled
with a lot of people that will tell you things

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.060
that make no sense.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.200
He's definitely one of them.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.200
Just ignore him.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.460
Bad Voice: Are you kidding me?

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.650
Do I really have to sit here and listen to
your bullshit you keep feeding him?

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:11.120
Listen, every single entrepreneur that became
wealthy, comes from a family that had millions

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.240
of dollars to back them up.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.360
Do you think he's got money to back him up
and go out there and become successful?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.810
Stop feeding him this kind of crap, man.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.080
He's working way too hard.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.140
The guy's working 80 hours a week.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.440
He should be staying home and relaxing.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.950
That's way too much work for him.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:24.950
Good Voice: Oh yeah?

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.560
So what would you rather have him do?

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.560
Watch TV?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.130
Watch sports?

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.350
Watch the news?

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.520
Do all that sort of thing?

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.520
Bad Voice: Yes!

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.520
Of course.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.520
That's what normal people do.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.520
My gosh.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.160
Good Voice: No, no.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.140
That's what people with no purpose do.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.200
Bad Voice: So let me get this straight.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.230
Are you trying to say that I have no purpose?

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.440
Good Voice: You may not have a purpose, but
that's not what I'm really saying.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.930
What I'm trying to tell you is, when people
actually get clear about what they want in

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.340
their lives, the value of time goes higher.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.600
You don't value your time.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.160
He's trying to value his time.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.280
Bad Voice: [Chuckles] Look at this guy to
my right.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.900
Look at the way he's looking at me like as if he's
better than me, driving a red Ferrari.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.900
What are you looking at?

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.840
Who would drive a red Ferrari in the first
place?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:13.840
Drive off!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.650
Good Voice: It's actually a pretty nice Ferrari
he's got.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.420
Bad Voice: You know what we should do?

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.870
You know the girl we met this past weekend.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:22.870
What was her name?

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:23.870
Uh, Rach.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.870
. Rachel?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:25.870
Um, Rochelle?

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:26.870
Roxie!

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:27.870
We should call Roxie right now.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:28.870
That's what we should do.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.890
Good Voice: We don't need to do that, Pat.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.920
You got bigger and better things to do right
now.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.150
Let's just stay focused.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.300
Bad Voice: Just stop already, man.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.360
Stop!

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.630
Man, what happened to Pops when he started
a business?

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.540
He failed!

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.120
What happened to Mom and Dad?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.680
They got a divorce!

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.680
What happened to us?

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.040
We lived six different places.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.420
Was it fun?

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.090
Hell no, it wasn't fun.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.790
What happened in high school to you?

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.200
Did you play baseball?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.340
Did you play high school basketball?

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.180
Did you get picked up for football?

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.180
Did you date the girl you liked?

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.180
What was your GPA?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.600
Who were you in high school?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.700
Who were you afterwards?

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.410
What makes you think you are going to make
it in life?

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.850
You've got to stop selling this stuff to this
guy, man.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.720
Stop it!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.900
It's getting old!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.920
Go get that job that you let go of, paying you twelve bucks an hour

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.120
and part-time, get a degree.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.100
Stop taking these damn risks.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.790
We're not meant to do something big with our
lives.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.030
Simple as that.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.160
Good Voice: Are we done?

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.940
I'm done, I'm good.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.540
Good Voice: Okay, good.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.020
Pat, I want you to know, this voice is never
going away.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.260
This voice is always going to be there, no
matter how much money you're going to make,

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.150
it's always going to be there.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:49.530
The great thing about it though, every morning
you wake up, you have a choice

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.300
on which voice to listen to.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.660
But I want you to think about a completely
different thing right now.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.460
Let's just say you do nothing.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.660
Let's just say that you buy into your fears.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:01.230
Let's just say that you buy into every single
thing you're worried about.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.670
Let's just say you don't make any decisions
to go after your dreams.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:08.180
Fast forward 10 years from now, 20 years from
now, 30 years from now, 40 years from now.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.970
Let's just say you're funeral's around the
corner.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.060
You have 50 people there, 100 people there.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.520
Maybe 200 people show up.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.560
These are your friends, family and people
that love you.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.541
See, you'll be loved for one generation, remembered
for two generations, and forgotten after that.

00:05:21.541 --> 00:05:23.690
Is that truly the life you want to live?

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.340
Is that really what you want to do?

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.170
I don't know if that's the life you really
want to live.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:32.760
You see, what I've noticed is no matter what
you do, you'll have a lot of lonely times.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.550
You can lie to your family.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:35.550
You can lie to your friends.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:39.700
You can fool the world into realizing that
why you didn't win was because of some challenge

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.970
you had to face.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:43.280
But there is one person you can never lie
to.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.410
And that is the man in the mirror.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.690
You can never lie to the man in the mirror.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:48.690
Never.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:52.770
For the rest of your life, the man in the
mirror is going to look back at you and say,

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.520
"You did not choose to go after your dreams."

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.380
And you have to be okay with that.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.139
Now, what I would like to encourage you to
do is to make the right choice.

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:05.710
I encourage you to face your fears and pursue
your dreams.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.580
Go pursue the dreams that matter the most
to you.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.080
You've only got one shot at this thing here.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:13.260
And if it works out, man, it's going to feel
so good for you.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.860
And if it doesn't, at least you had the courage
to make that decision.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.320
I hope you make the right choice.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.600
I trust you will.

